comments.text:
정정 — 바로 앞 코멘트에서 코드 인용이 통째로 사라졌다

앞 코멘트의 「master app.js .」 자리에 있어야 할 인용이다. 백틱으로 감싼 채 셸 인자로
넘겨 명령 치환이 먹었다(리더가 msg-df16a042b7c8 계열에서 말한 사고와 같은 형태다).
아래는 파일로 붙인 것이라 온전하다.

master 9938206, src/claude_launcher/web/static/app.js, syncSpawnGates 안:

    const childHarness = String((ui.harness && ui.harness.value) || "") ||
      (pickedDetail ? pickedDetail.harness : (ui.parentSess || {}).harness || "");
    const nonClaude = !!childHarness && childHarness !== "claude";
    if (nonClaude) {
      lock(ui.nullTok, ui.nullNote, "the claude harness only");
    }

409i의 base(152624a)에서는 첫 줄이 이랬다:

    const childHarness = pickedDetail
      ? pickedDetail.harness : (ui.parentSess || {}).harness || "";

즉 출처가 셋이 됐고 명시 피커가 가장 앞선다. 같은 nonClaude가 fork 행도 잠근다.

부수 확인 하나(s181과 s244가 각각 열어 둔 항목): ka65가 더한 lock 호출의 대상
ui.harness는 select다 — master app.js:13052

    ui.harness = document.createElement("select");

그러므로 696c1fb의 절(field.type === "checkbox"일 때만 체크를 지운다)은 그 호출에
발화하지 않는다. 간극의 크기는 그만큼 줄고, 남는 것은 childHarness 입력 경로 둘이다.

절차 메모: 코드를 담은 beads 코멘트는 인자가 아니라 파일로 붙인다
(claunch beads comments add <id> -f <파일>).

줄 번호를 붙입니다 — s244 가 관측했고, master 323fc89 축에서 직접 확인했습니다.

    src/claude_launcher/web/static/app.js @ 323fc89

    12589  const childHarness = String((ui.harness && ui.harness.value) || "") ||
    12590    (pickedDetail ? pickedDetail.harness : (ui.parentSess || {}).harness || "");
    ...
    12593  if (ui.harness) {
    12594    lock(ui.harness, ui.harnessNote, may.includes("profile") ? "" :
    12595      "the child runs under its parent's harness (spawn.allow_profile)");
    12596  }
    ...
    12763  if (!ui.profile.disabled && (!ui.harness || !ui.harness.disabled)) {
    12764    put("profile", spawnProfileOverride(ui));
    12765  }

12589 의 childHarness 읽기에는 12763 이 하는 .disabled 확인이 없습니다. 12594 에서
ui.harness 가 잠겨도 select 의 값은 남으므로(잠금이 값을 지우는 것은 체크박스뿐입니다),
사용자가 고를 수도 없고 페이로드에도 실리지 않을 하네스 값이 계속 nonClaude 를 참으로
만들어 nullTok 과 fork 행을 잠급니다.

이 줄들은 claunch-409i 의 델타 밖에 있는 master 코드이므로 그 착지를 막지 않습니다.
이 이슈에서 다룰 커버리지 공백과 같은 자리입니다: childHarness 의 입력 경로가 셋인데
(명시적 하네스 선택기, pickedDetail.harness + baseProfileName 폴백, 부모의 하네스)
tests/web/spawnmodal_check.js 의 기존 체크가 지나는 것은 부모 경로 하나뿐입니다.

관측자는 s244, 줄 번호 확인은 s245.

/* Render one of app.js's drawing functions at two git refs and put the two
   results side by side on a page a PERSON can look at.

   Why this exists. The dashboard has no build step and no browser in the
   loop, so a change to a drawing function is verified by counting
   coordinates in the SVG it emits. That catches "two labels share an (x,y)"
   and never catches "this reads worse than before". Three sessions in one
   shift reported the same blank honestly — nobody had seen the thing they
   changed — and the answer was always "please look at it", addressed to a
   person with no page to look at. This builds that page.

   What it does NOT do: rasterize. Installing a rasterizer into a checkout
   that a dozen sessions share is out of scope for a UI round, and it is not
   needed — the artifact viewer is a browser, so inlining the SVG and the
   dashboard's own rules renders the real thing.

     node render_diff.js <config.json> <out.html>

   The dashboard's styles are LIFTED FROM style.css by selector prefix, not
   copied into this file. That distinction is the whole point: hand-copied
   styles drift, and a page whose styles drifted answers "it looked fine on
   that page", which is not the question being asked.

   ── config ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   repo          repo root (default: cwd)
   source        the JS file to slice from      (default: app.js)
   stylesheet    the CSS file to lift from      (default: style.css)
   stylePrefixes selector prefixes to lift, e.g. [".wfd"]
   slices        how to cut the functions out of `source`. Two forms, both
                 already used by tests/web/*_check.js:
                   {"span": ["function escXml(", "@RULE"]}   from .. to
                   {"fn": "wfDiagramSvg"}                    brace-matched
                 "@RULE" expands to the file's section-rule comment.
   exports       names the slices define that `render` needs
   fixture       inline object, or {"file": "..."} — bound as `fixture`
   render        a JS expression returning an HTML/SVG STRING
   panels        [{tag, label, ref}] — ref is a git ref, or "WORKTREE" for
                 the working copy. Usually exactly two.
   ── everything below is page copy, all optional ─────────────────────────
   title heading eyebrow standfirst ident deltas looks table sections
   caveats

   A page with no `deltas`/`looks`/`table` is still a valid page: two
   renderings and a caveat. Do not invent findings to fill a section.

   ── limits, and they are real ───────────────────────────────────────────
   · `render` must return a string. A function that writes into the DOM
     needs the stub-DOM harness that tests/web/render_check.js builds; this
     script does not carry one.
   · Two static pictures show what a thing LOOKS like, never what it DOES.
     A toggle's two glyphs can sit side by side; "it toggles when clicked"
     cannot be drawn. Say so in `caveats` rather than implying otherwise —
     the page is worth less than nothing if it lets a reader believe an
     interaction was checked.
*/
"use strict";

const fs = require("fs");
const path = require("path");
const cp = require("child_process");

const RULE = "/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */";

const [, , configPath, outPath] = process.argv;
if (!configPath || !outPath) {
  console.error("usage: node render_diff.js <config.json> <out.html>");
  process.exit(2);
}
const cfg = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(configPath, "utf8"));
const repo = path.resolve(cfg.repo || process.cwd());
const SRC = cfg.source || "src/claude_launcher/web/static/app.js";
const CSS = cfg.stylesheet || "src/claude_launcher/web/static/style.css";

/* ---- reading a file at a ref ------------------------------------------ */

function at(ref, rel) {
  if (ref === "WORKTREE") return fs.readFileSync(path.join(repo, rel), "utf8");
  return cp.execSync(`git show ${ref}:${rel}`, { cwd: repo, maxBuffer: 1 << 28 })
    .toString("utf8");
}

/* ---- cutting the functions out ---------------------------------------- */

function cutSpan(src, from, to) {
  const a = src.indexOf(from === "@RULE" ? RULE : from);
  const b = src.indexOf(to === "@RULE" ? RULE : to, a + 1);
  if (a < 0 || b < 0 || b <= a) throw new Error(`cannot slice ${from} .. ${to}`);
  return src.slice(a, b);
}

/* Brace-matched from `function <name>(`, the way rolepanel_check slices. */
function cutFn(src, name) {
  const head = src.indexOf(`function ${name}(`);
  if (head < 0) throw new Error(`no function ${name}`);
  let depth = 0;
  for (let j = src.indexOf("{", head); j < src.length; j++) {
    if (src[j] === "{") depth++;
    else if (src[j] === "}") { if (!--depth) return src.slice(head, j + 1); }
  }
  throw new Error(`unbalanced ${name}`);
}

function buildContext(src) {
  const code = (cfg.slices || []).map((s) =>
    s.fn ? cutFn(src, s.fn) : cutSpan(src, s.span[0], s.span[1])).join("\n");
  const names = cfg.exports || [];
  const ctx = {};
  new Function("exports", `${code}\nObject.assign(exports, {${names.join(",")}});`)(ctx);
  return ctx;
}

/* ---- lifting the real styles ------------------------------------------ */

/* A deliberately small CSS scanner: walk top-level rules, recurse into
   at-rules, keep any rule whose selector list mentions one of the prefixes.
   It does not need to understand CSS — only to find rule boundaries. */
function liftStyles(css, prefixes) {
  const kept = [];
  const walk = (text) => {
    let i = 0;
    while (i < text.length) {
      const open = text.indexOf("{", i);
      if (open < 0) break;
      let depth = 1, j = open + 1;
      for (; j < text.length && depth; j++) {
        if (text[j] === "{") depth++;
        else if (text[j] === "}") depth--;
      }
      const selector = text.slice(i, open).trim();
      const body = text.slice(open + 1, j - 1);
      if (selector.startsWith("@")) walk(body);            // @media, @supports
      else if (prefixes.some((p) => selector.includes(p))) {
        kept.push(`${selector} { ${body.trim()} }`);
      }
      i = j;
    }
  };
  walk(stripComments(css));
  return kept;
}

function stripComments(s) { return s.replace(/\/\*[\s\S]*?\*\//g, ""); }

/* SVG text carries no font of its own — in the dashboard it inherits from
   `body`, and lifting only the prefixed rules leaves it on the browser's
   default face. That is not a styling nicety: a specimen set in the wrong
   type is not the thing being inspected. Take the dashboard's own stack. */
function liftBodyFont(css) {
  const body = stripComments(css).match(/(^|})\s*body\s*{([^}]*)}/);
  const decl = body && body[2].match(/font-family\s*:\s*([^;}]+)/);
  return decl ? decl[1].trim() : null;
}

/* ---- rendering each panel --------------------------------------------- */

/* Two SVGs on one page must not share element ids: the second one's
   `url(#arrow)` would resolve against the first one's defs. Give each panel
   its own suffix. */
function isolateIds(html, suffix) {
  const ids = [...html.matchAll(/\sid="([^"]+)"/g)].map((m) => m[1]);
  let out = html;
  for (const id of new Set(ids)) {
    const q = id.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, "\\$&");
    out = out.replace(new RegExp(`\\sid="${q}"`, "g"), ` id="${id}-${suffix}"`)
             .replace(new RegExp(`url\\(#${q}\\)`, "g"), `url(#${id}-${suffix})`);
  }
  return out;
}

const fixture = cfg.fixture && cfg.fixture.file
  ? JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(path.dirname(configPath), cfg.fixture.file), "utf8"))
  : cfg.fixture;

const panels = (cfg.panels || []).map((p) => {
  const ctx = buildContext(at(p.ref, SRC));
  const args = Object.keys(ctx);
  const html = new Function(...args, "fixture", `return (${cfg.render});`)(
    ...args.map((k) => ctx[k]), fixture);
  if (typeof html !== "string") {
    throw new Error(`render must return a string; got ${typeof html}. ` +
      "A function that writes into the DOM needs a stub-DOM harness, which " +
      "this script does not carry.");
  }
  return { ...p, html: isolateIds(html, p.tag) };
});

const css = at(panels[panels.length - 1].ref, CSS);
const lifted = liftStyles(css, cfg.stylePrefixes || []);
const bodyFont = liftBodyFont(css);

/* ---- the page ---------------------------------------------------------- */

const esc = (s) => String(s).replace(/&/g, "&amp;").replace(/</g, "&lt;")
  .replace(/>/g, "&gt;").replace(/"/g, "&quot;");

const CHROME = fs.readFileSync(path.join(__dirname, "chrome.css"), "utf8");

const parts = [];
parts.push(`<title>${esc(cfg.title || "before / after")}</title>`);
parts.push('<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">');
parts.push('<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>');
parts.push('<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?' +
  'family=Archivo:wght@500;600;700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600' +
  '&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">');
parts.push(`<style>\n${CHROME}\n`);
parts.push("/* lifted verbatim from " + CSS + " — not a copy kept in step by hand */");
if (bodyFont) parts.push(`.mount { font-family: ${bodyFont}; }`);
parts.push(lifted.join("\n"));
parts.push("</style>");

parts.push('<div class="wrap">');

parts.push('<header class="mast">');
if (cfg.eyebrow) parts.push(`<p class="eyebrow">${esc(cfg.eyebrow)}</p>`);
parts.push(`<h1>${cfg.heading || esc(cfg.title || "")}</h1>`);
if (cfg.standfirst) parts.push(`<p class="standfirst">${cfg.standfirst}</p>`);
if (cfg.ident) {
  parts.push('<p class="ident">' + cfg.ident
    .map(([k, v]) => `<span><b>${esc(k)}</b> ${esc(v)}</span>`).join("") + "</p>");
}
parts.push("</header>");

if (cfg.deltas && cfg.deltas.length) {
  parts.push('<section class="deltas" aria-label="측정된 변화">');
  for (const d of cfg.deltas) {
    parts.push('<div class="delta">' +
      `<span class="delta-name">${esc(d.name)}</span>` +
      '<span class="delta-nums">' +
      `<span class="delta-was">${esc(d.was)}</span>` +
      '<span class="delta-arrow">→</span>' +
      `<span class="delta-now">${esc(d.now)}</span></span>` +
      (d.note ? `<span class="delta-note">${d.note}</span>` : "") + "</div>");
  }
  parts.push("</section>");
}

parts.push("<section>");
parts.push(`<h2>${esc(cfg.panelsHeading || "같은 입력, 같은 배율")}</h2>`);
parts.push('<div class="pair">');
for (const p of panels) {
  parts.push('<figure class="specimen">');
  parts.push('<figcaption class="specimen-head">' +
    `<span class="tag ${esc(p.tag)}">${esc(p.label || p.tag)}</span>` +
    `<code>${esc(p.ref)}</code></figcaption>`);
  parts.push(`<div class="mount">${p.html}</div>`);
  parts.push("</figure>");
}
parts.push("</div></section>");

if (cfg.looks && cfg.looks.length) {
  parts.push("<section>");
  parts.push(`<h2>${esc(cfg.looksHeading || "어디를 볼 것인가")}</h2>`);
  parts.push('<div class="looks">');
  for (const l of cfg.looks) {
    parts.push('<div class="look">' +
      `<div class="look-where">${l.where || ""}</div><div>` +
      `<h3>${l.title}</h3>${(l.body || []).join("")}</div></div>`);
  }
  parts.push("</div></section>");
}

for (const s of cfg.sections || []) {
  parts.push("<section>");
  if (s.heading) parts.push(`<h2>${esc(s.heading)}</h2>`);
  parts.push(s.html);
  parts.push("</section>");
}

if (cfg.table) {
  parts.push("<section>");
  parts.push(`<h2>${esc(cfg.table.heading || "측정한 축")}</h2>`);
  parts.push('<div class="tablewrap"><table>');
  if (cfg.table.caption) parts.push(`<caption>${cfg.table.caption}</caption>`);
  parts.push("<thead><tr>" +
    cfg.table.head.map((h) => `<th>${h}</th>`).join("") + "</tr></thead><tbody>");
  for (const row of cfg.table.rows) {
    parts.push("<tr>" + row.map((cell, i) => {
      if (i === 0) return `<td>${cell}</td>`;
      const cls = cfg.table.classes ? cfg.table.classes[i] || "n" : "n";
      return `<td class="${cls}">${cell}</td>`;
    }).join("") + "</tr>");
  }
  parts.push("</tbody></table></div></section>");
}

if (cfg.caveats) {
  parts.push('<section><div class="caveat">');
  parts.push(`<h2>${esc(cfg.caveats.title || "이 페이지가 말해 주지 못하는 것")}</h2>`);
  if (cfg.caveats.intro) parts.push(`<p>${cfg.caveats.intro}</p>`);
  if (cfg.caveats.items && cfg.caveats.items.length) {
    parts.push("<ul>" + cfg.caveats.items.map((i) => `<li>${i}</li>`).join("") + "</ul>");
  }
  parts.push("</div></section>");
}

parts.push("</div>");

fs.writeFileSync(outPath, parts.join("\n"));
console.log(`${outPath}: ${panels.length} panel(s) ` +
  `[${panels.map((p) => `${p.tag}@${p.ref}`).join(", ")}], ` +
  `${lifted.length} rule(s) lifted from ${path.basename(CSS)}`);

/* Page chrome for render_diff.js. The dashboard's own rules are lifted from
   style.css and appended after this block — nothing here may style the
   specimen itself, or the page stops showing the real thing. */

:root {
  /* Neutrals biased toward the dashboard's slate rather than a flat grey */
  --ground:      #e9edf2;
  --surface:     #ffffff;
  --edge:        #cfd7e0;
  --ink:         #151a21;
  --ink-soft:    #4d5866;
  --ink-faint:   #77828f;

  /* The mount stays dark in both themes: the specimen is being inspected as
     it appears in the dashboard, not restyled to suit this page. */
  --mount:       #0f1216;
  --mount-edge:  #262c35;

  /* Semantic, borrowed from the dashboard's own vocabulary — amber is what
     it marks a repeated visit with, green a visited step. Before / after. */
  --was:         #b07d13;
  --was-ground:  #fdf4e0;
  --now:         #1f7a42;
  --now-ground:  #e3f4e9;

  --rule:        #dbe2ea;
  --shadow:      0 1px 2px rgba(21, 26, 33, .06), 0 8px 24px -12px rgba(21, 26, 33, .18);

  --font-display: "Archivo", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
  --font-body:    "IBM Plex Sans", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
  --font-mono:    "IBM Plex Mono", ui-monospace, "Cascadia Mono", Consolas, monospace;
}

@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
    --ground:     #0c0f13;
    --surface:    #14181e;
    --edge:       #262d36;
    --ink:        #dde3ea;
    --ink-soft:   #98a3b1;
    --ink-faint:  #6d7783;
    --mount:      #0f1216;
    --mount-edge: #2b323c;
    --was:        #d29922;
    --was-ground: #2a2113;
    --now:        #46a869;
    --now-ground: #14261b;
    --rule:       #232a33;
    --shadow:     0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, .5), 0 10px 28px -14px rgba(0, 0, 0, .7);
  }
}
:root[data-theme="dark"] {
  --ground:     #0c0f13;
  --surface:    #14181e;
  --edge:       #262d36;
  --ink:        #dde3ea;
  --ink-soft:   #98a3b1;
  --ink-faint:  #6d7783;
  --mount:      #0f1216;
  --mount-edge: #2b323c;
  --was:        #d29922;
  --was-ground: #2a2113;
  --now:        #46a869;
  --now-ground: #14261b;
  --rule:       #232a33;
  --shadow:     0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, .5), 0 10px 28px -14px rgba(0, 0, 0, .7);
}

*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }

body {
  margin: 0;
  background: var(--ground);
  color: var(--ink);
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: 15px;
  line-height: 1.6;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}

.wrap {
  max-width: 1120px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 56px 28px 96px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 56px;
}

/* ---- masthead ---------------------------------------------------------- */

.mast { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; }

.eyebrow {
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 11.5px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: .13em;
  text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-faint); margin: 0;
}

.mast h1 {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: clamp(30px, 4.4vw, 46px);
  font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.022em; line-height: 1.1;
  text-wrap: balance; margin: 0; max-width: 20ch;
}

.standfirst { margin: 0; max-width: 66ch; font-size: 17px; color: var(--ink-soft); }

.ident {
  display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 20px;
  padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-faint);
  margin: 0;
}
.ident b { color: var(--ink-soft); font-weight: 500; }

/* ---- measured deltas --------------------------------------------------- */

.deltas {
  display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr));
  gap: 1px; background: var(--edge); border: 1px solid var(--edge);
  border-radius: 3px; overflow: hidden;
}

.delta {
  background: var(--surface); padding: 20px 22px 22px;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 9px;
}
.delta-name { font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.35; }
.delta-nums {
  display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 9px;
  font-family: var(--font-mono); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
.delta-was { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--was); }
.delta-now { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--now); }
.delta-arrow { font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink-faint); }
.delta-note { font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-faint); line-height: 1.45; }

/* ---- section headings -------------------------------------------------- */

.wrap > section > h2 {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-faint); margin: 0 0 20px;
  padding-bottom: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
}

/* ---- specimens --------------------------------------------------------- */

.pair {
  display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(340px, 1fr));
  gap: 24px;
}

.specimen {
  margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column;
  border: 1px solid var(--edge); border-radius: 3px;
  background: var(--surface); box-shadow: var(--shadow); overflow: hidden;
}

.specimen-head {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;
  padding: 13px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--edge);
}
.specimen-head code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-faint); }

.tag {
  font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10.5px; font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: .09em; text-transform: uppercase;
  padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 2px;
  color: var(--ink-soft); background: var(--ground);
}
.tag.before, .tag.was { color: var(--was); background: var(--was-ground); }
.tag.after,  .tag.now { color: var(--now); background: var(--now-ground); }

.mount {
  background: var(--mount); border-top: 1px solid var(--mount-edge);
  padding: 18px 8px 24px; overflow-x: auto;
  display: flex; justify-content: center;
}
.mount svg { display: block; max-width: 100%; height: auto; }

/* ---- what to look at --------------------------------------------------- */

.looks {
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1px; background: var(--edge);
  border: 1px solid var(--edge); border-radius: 3px; overflow: hidden;
}
.look {
  background: var(--surface); display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 46px 1fr; gap: 0 18px; padding: 20px 22px;
}
.look-where {
  font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--ink-faint); letter-spacing: .04em; padding-top: 3px; line-height: 1.35;
}
.look h3 {
  font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: -.008em; margin: 0 0 6px; color: var(--ink);
}
.look p { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 68ch; }
.look p + p { margin-top: 7px; }
.look code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .92em; }
.num { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }

/* ---- tables ------------------------------------------------------------ */

.tablewrap {
  overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--edge);
  border-radius: 3px; background: var(--surface);
}
.tablewrap table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 14px; }
.tablewrap caption {
  text-align: left; padding: 16px 20px 0; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-faint);
}
.tablewrap th, .tablewrap td {
  padding: 11px 20px; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
}
.tablewrap thead th {
  font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-faint);
}
.tablewrap tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
.tablewrap td.n {
  font-family: var(--font-mono); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap;
}
.tablewrap td.n.was { color: var(--was); }
.tablewrap td.n.now { color: var(--now); font-weight: 500; }
.tablewrap code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .92em; }

/* ---- caveat ------------------------------------------------------------ */

.caveat {
  border: 1px solid var(--edge); border-left: 3px solid var(--was);
  border-radius: 3px; background: var(--surface); padding: 24px 26px;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px;
}
.caveat.settled { border-left-color: var(--now); }
.caveat h2 {
  font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: -.01em; margin: 0; border: 0; padding: 0;
  text-transform: none; letter-spacing: -.01em; color: var(--ink);
}
.caveat p { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 72ch; }
.caveat ul {
  margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 7px;
}
.caveat li { font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 70ch; }
.caveat code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .92em; }
.caveat .tablewrap { border: 0; }

a { color: inherit; }
a:focus-visible, [tabindex]:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--now); outline-offset: 2px;
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  * { animation: none !important; transition: none !important; }
}

/* Render one of app.js's drawing functions at two git refs and put the two
   results side by side on a page a PERSON can look at.

   Why this exists. The dashboard has no build step and no browser in the
   loop, so a change to a drawing function is verified by counting
   coordinates in the SVG it emits. That catches "two labels share an (x,y)"
   and never catches "this reads worse than before". Three sessions in one
   shift reported the same blank honestly — nobody had seen the thing they
   changed — and the answer was always "please look at it", addressed to a
   person with no page to look at. This builds that page.

   What it does NOT do: rasterize. Installing a rasterizer into a checkout
   that a dozen sessions share is out of scope for a UI round, and it is not
   needed — the artifact viewer is a browser, so inlining the SVG and the
   dashboard's own rules renders the real thing.

     node render_diff.js <config.json> <out.html>

   The dashboard's styles are LIFTED FROM style.css by selector prefix, not
   copied into this file. That distinction is the whole point: hand-copied
   styles drift, and a page whose styles drifted answers "it looked fine on
   that page", which is not the question being asked.

   ── config ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   repo          repo root (default: cwd)
   source        the JS file to slice from      (default: app.js)
   stylesheet    the CSS file to lift from      (default: style.css)
   stylePrefixes selector prefixes to lift, e.g. [".wfd"]
   slices        how to cut the functions out of `source`. Two forms, both
                 already used by tests/web/*_check.js:
                   {"span": ["function escXml(", "@RULE"]}   from .. to
                   {"fn": "wfDiagramSvg"}                    brace-matched
                 "@RULE" expands to the file's section-rule comment.
                 PREFER span. Brace matching does not know it is inside a
                 string or a regex literal, so a function containing `}` in
                 one — `/[^;}]+/`, `"}"` — is cut short and the slice fails
                 to parse. The repo's own rolepanel_check slices by name and
                 carries the same hazard; this file's helpers hit it, which
                 is why csslift_check slices them by span.
   exports       names the slices define that `render` needs
   fixture       inline object, or {"file": "..."} — bound as `fixture`
   render        a JS expression returning an HTML/SVG STRING
   panels        [{tag, label, ref}] — ref is a git ref, or "WORKTREE" for
                 the working copy. Usually exactly two.
   ── everything below is page copy, all optional ─────────────────────────
   title heading eyebrow standfirst ident deltas looks table sections
   caveats

   A page with no `deltas`/`looks`/`table` is still a valid page: two
   renderings and a caveat. Do not invent findings to fill a section.

   ── limits, and they are real ───────────────────────────────────────────
   · `render` must return a string. A function that writes into the DOM
     needs the stub-DOM harness that tests/web/render_check.js builds; this
     script does not carry one.
   · Two static pictures show what a thing LOOKS like, never what it DOES.
     A toggle's two glyphs can sit side by side; "it toggles when clicked"
     cannot be drawn. Say so in `caveats` rather than implying otherwise —
     the page is worth less than nothing if it lets a reader believe an
     interaction was checked.
*/
"use strict";

const fs = require("fs");
const path = require("path");
const cp = require("child_process");

const RULE = "/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */";

const [, , configPath, outPath] = process.argv;
if (!configPath || !outPath) {
  console.error("usage: node render_diff.js <config.json> <out.html>");
  process.exit(2);
}
const cfg = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(configPath, "utf8"));
const repo = path.resolve(cfg.repo || process.cwd());
const SRC = cfg.source || "src/claude_launcher/web/static/app.js";
const CSS = cfg.stylesheet || "src/claude_launcher/web/static/style.css";

/* ---- reading a file at a ref ------------------------------------------ */

function at(ref, rel) {
  if (ref === "WORKTREE") return fs.readFileSync(path.join(repo, rel), "utf8");
  return cp.execSync(`git show ${ref}:${rel}`, { cwd: repo, maxBuffer: 1 << 28 })
    .toString("utf8");
}

/* ---- cutting the functions out ---------------------------------------- */

function cutSpan(src, from, to) {
  const a = src.indexOf(from === "@RULE" ? RULE : from);
  const b = src.indexOf(to === "@RULE" ? RULE : to, a + 1);
  if (a < 0 || b < 0 || b <= a) throw new Error(`cannot slice ${from} .. ${to}`);
  return src.slice(a, b);
}

/* Brace-matched from `function <name>(`, the way rolepanel_check slices. */
function cutFn(src, name) {
  const head = src.indexOf(`function ${name}(`);
  if (head < 0) throw new Error(`no function ${name}`);
  let depth = 0;
  for (let j = src.indexOf("{", head); j < src.length; j++) {
    if (src[j] === "{") depth++;
    else if (src[j] === "}") { if (!--depth) return src.slice(head, j + 1); }
  }
  throw new Error(`unbalanced ${name}`);
}

function buildContext(src) {
  const code = (cfg.slices || []).map((s) =>
    s.fn ? cutFn(src, s.fn) : cutSpan(src, s.span[0], s.span[1])).join("\n");
  const names = cfg.exports || [];
  const ctx = {};
  new Function("exports", `${code}\nObject.assign(exports, {${names.join(",")}});`)(ctx);
  return ctx;
}

/* ---- lifting the real styles ------------------------------------------ */

/* A deliberately small CSS scanner: walk top-level rules, recurse into
   at-rules, keep any rule whose selector list mentions one of the prefixes.
   It does not need to understand CSS — only to find rule boundaries.

   A rule nested in an at-rule is NOT lifted, and that is a decision, not an
   oversight. Lifting it flat is the worst of the three options and is what
   this function did until s169 measured it: `@media (max-width: 820px) {
   #term-header { display: none } }` came out unconditional and produced a
   page with the specimen missing entirely. Keeping the wrapper is barely
   better — the condition would then be about THIS page's viewport, and the
   specimen sits in a mount rather than at the dashboard's full width, so
   the condition no longer means what it meant. So the default is to leave
   them, `liftAtRules` takes them (wrapper intact) when an author decides
   the condition does carry over, and either way the count comes back to the
   caller. What must never happen is the third thing: dropping them
   quietly, which hands the reader a specimen that is missing rules and
   says nothing. A page that misleads is worth less than no page. */
function liftStyles(css, prefixes, liftAtRules) {
  const kept = [], skipped = [];
  const walk = (text, enclosing) => {
    let i = 0;
    while (i < text.length) {
      const open = text.indexOf("{", i);
      if (open < 0) break;
      let depth = 1, j = open + 1;
      for (; j < text.length && depth; j++) {
        if (text[j] === "{") depth++;
        else if (text[j] === "}") depth--;
      }
      const selector = text.slice(i, open).trim();
      const body = text.slice(open + 1, j - 1);
      if (selector.startsWith("@")) walk(body, enclosing.concat(selector));
      else if (prefixes.some((p) => selector.includes(p))) {
        const rule = `${selector} { ${body.trim()} }`;
        if (!enclosing.length) kept.push(rule);
        else if (liftAtRules) {
          kept.push(`${enclosing.join(" { ")} { ${rule} ${"}".repeat(enclosing.length)}`);
        } else skipped.push({ at: enclosing.join(" "), selector });
      }
      i = j;
    }
  };
  walk(stripComments(css), []);
  return { kept, skipped };
}

function stripComments(s) { return s.replace(/\/\*[\s\S]*?\*\//g, ""); }

/* SVG text carries no font of its own — in the dashboard it inherits from
   `body`, and lifting only the prefixed rules leaves it on the browser's
   default face. That is not a styling nicety: a specimen set in the wrong
   type is not the thing being inspected. Take the dashboard's own stack. */
function liftBodyFont(css) {
  const body = stripComments(css).match(/(^|})\s*body\s*{([^}]*)}/);
  // `[^;]` and not `[^;}]`: the captured body already stops at the brace, and
  // a `}` inside this literal breaks anything that slices functions by
  // brace-matching — which is how this file's own `cutFn` and the repo's
  // rolepanel_check both read source. Cheap to avoid, annoying to debug.
  const decl = body && body[2].match(/font-family\s*:\s*([^;]+)/);
  return decl ? decl[1].trim() : null;
}

/* ---- rendering each panel --------------------------------------------- */

/* Two SVGs on one page must not share element ids: the second one's
   `url(#arrow)` would resolve against the first one's defs. Give each panel
   its own suffix. */
function isolateIds(html, suffix) {
  const ids = [...html.matchAll(/\sid="([^"]+)"/g)].map((m) => m[1]);
  let out = html;
  for (const id of new Set(ids)) {
    const q = id.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, "\\$&");
    out = out.replace(new RegExp(`\\sid="${q}"`, "g"), ` id="${id}-${suffix}"`)
             .replace(new RegExp(`url\\(#${q}\\)`, "g"), `url(#${id}-${suffix})`);
  }
  return out;
}

const fixture = cfg.fixture && cfg.fixture.file
  ? JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(path.dirname(configPath), cfg.fixture.file), "utf8"))
  : cfg.fixture;

const panels = (cfg.panels || []).map((p) => {
  const ctx = buildContext(at(p.ref, SRC));
  const args = Object.keys(ctx);
  const html = new Function(...args, "fixture", `return (${cfg.render});`)(
    ...args.map((k) => ctx[k]), fixture);
  if (typeof html !== "string") {
    throw new Error(`render must return a string; got ${typeof html}. ` +
      "A function that writes into the DOM needs a stub-DOM harness, which " +
      "this script does not carry.");
  }
  return { ...p, html: isolateIds(html, p.tag) };
});

const css = at(panels[panels.length - 1].ref, CSS);
const { kept: lifted, skipped } = liftStyles(css, cfg.stylePrefixes || [],
                                             cfg.liftAtRules);
const bodyFont = liftBodyFont(css);

/* A tripwire, not a checklist (s169's shape, and it is the better one): name
   the selectors the specimen cannot be read without, and let generation FAIL
   when one stops arriving. A list that is merely printed shrinks quietly the
   day someone renames a class. */
const missing = (cfg.requireSelectors || []).filter(
  (want) => !lifted.some((rule) => rule.slice(0, rule.indexOf("{")).includes(want)));
if (missing.length) {
  console.error(`render_diff: required selector(s) not lifted from ${CSS}: ` +
    missing.join(", ") + "\n  the specimen would be drawn without them — " +
    "check stylePrefixes, or whether the rule moved into an at-rule.");
  process.exit(1);
}

/* ---- the page ---------------------------------------------------------- */

const esc = (s) => String(s).replace(/&/g, "&amp;").replace(/</g, "&lt;")
  .replace(/>/g, "&gt;").replace(/"/g, "&quot;");

const CHROME = fs.readFileSync(path.join(__dirname, "chrome.css"), "utf8");

const parts = [];
parts.push(`<title>${esc(cfg.title || "before / after")}</title>`);
parts.push('<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">');
parts.push('<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>');
parts.push('<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?' +
  'family=Archivo:wght@500;600;700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600' +
  '&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">');
parts.push(`<style>\n${CHROME}\n`);
parts.push("/* lifted verbatim from " + CSS + " — not a copy kept in step by hand */");
if (bodyFont) parts.push(`.mount { font-family: ${bodyFont}; }`);
parts.push(lifted.join("\n"));
parts.push("</style>");

parts.push('<div class="wrap">');

parts.push('<header class="mast">');
if (cfg.eyebrow) parts.push(`<p class="eyebrow">${esc(cfg.eyebrow)}</p>`);
parts.push(`<h1>${cfg.heading || esc(cfg.title || "")}</h1>`);
if (cfg.standfirst) parts.push(`<p class="standfirst">${cfg.standfirst}</p>`);
if (cfg.ident) {
  parts.push('<p class="ident">' + cfg.ident
    .map(([k, v]) => `<span><b>${esc(k)}</b> ${esc(v)}</span>`).join("") + "</p>");
}
parts.push("</header>");

if (cfg.deltas && cfg.deltas.length) {
  parts.push('<section class="deltas" aria-label="측정된 변화">');
  for (const d of cfg.deltas) {
    parts.push('<div class="delta">' +
      `<span class="delta-name">${esc(d.name)}</span>` +
      '<span class="delta-nums">' +
      `<span class="delta-was">${esc(d.was)}</span>` +
      '<span class="delta-arrow">→</span>' +
      `<span class="delta-now">${esc(d.now)}</span></span>` +
      (d.note ? `<span class="delta-note">${d.note}</span>` : "") + "</div>");
  }
  parts.push("</section>");
}

parts.push("<section>");
parts.push(`<h2>${esc(cfg.panelsHeading || "같은 입력, 같은 배율")}</h2>`);
parts.push('<div class="pair">');
for (const p of panels) {
  parts.push('<figure class="specimen">');
  parts.push('<figcaption class="specimen-head">' +
    `<span class="tag ${esc(p.tag)}">${esc(p.label || p.tag)}</span>` +
    `<code>${esc(p.ref)}</code></figcaption>`);
  parts.push(`<div class="mount">${p.html}</div>`);
  parts.push("</figure>");
}
parts.push("</div></section>");

if (cfg.looks && cfg.looks.length) {
  parts.push("<section>");
  parts.push(`<h2>${esc(cfg.looksHeading || "어디를 볼 것인가")}</h2>`);
  parts.push('<div class="looks">');
  for (const l of cfg.looks) {
    parts.push('<div class="look">' +
      `<div class="look-where">${l.where || ""}</div><div>` +
      `<h3>${l.title}</h3>${(l.body || []).join("")}</div></div>`);
  }
  parts.push("</div></section>");
}

for (const s of cfg.sections || []) {
  parts.push("<section>");
  if (s.heading) parts.push(`<h2>${esc(s.heading)}</h2>`);
  parts.push(s.html);
  parts.push("</section>");
}

if (cfg.table) {
  parts.push("<section>");
  parts.push(`<h2>${esc(cfg.table.heading || "측정한 축")}</h2>`);
  parts.push('<div class="tablewrap"><table>');
  if (cfg.table.caption) parts.push(`<caption>${cfg.table.caption}</caption>`);
  parts.push("<thead><tr>" +
    cfg.table.head.map((h) => `<th>${h}</th>`).join("") + "</tr></thead><tbody>");
  for (const row of cfg.table.rows) {
    parts.push("<tr>" + row.map((cell, i) => {
      if (i === 0) return `<td>${cell}</td>`;
      const cls = cfg.table.classes ? cfg.table.classes[i] || "n" : "n";
      return `<td class="${cls}">${cell}</td>`;
    }).join("") + "</tr>");
  }
  parts.push("</tbody></table></div></section>");
}

/* The caveat section is not optional, and neither is this line inside it:
   what the lift left behind is written by the TOOL, because an author who
   has to remember to write it is an author who will one day not. */
{
  const c = cfg.caveats || {};
  const items = (c.items || []).slice();
  items.push(`이 페이지의 표본 스타일은 <code>${esc(path.basename(CSS))}</code> 에서 ` +
    `<code>${(cfg.stylePrefixes || []).map(esc).join("</code> · <code>")}</code> 로 ` +
    `그때그때 뽑아 온다 — 손으로 베낀 사본이 아니다. 이번 생성에서 ` +
    `<strong class="num">${lifted.length}</strong>개 규칙을 가져왔다.`);
  if (skipped.length) {
    items.push(`<strong class="num">${skipped.length}</strong>개 규칙은 ` +
      `가져오지 않았다 — 조건부(at-rule) 안에 있고, 그 조건은 대시보드의 뷰포트에 ` +
      `대한 것이라 이 페이지에서는 같은 뜻이 아니다. 즉 <strong>이 표본은 ` +
      `무조건 규칙만 적용된 모습</strong>이다: ` +
      skipped.map((s) => `<code>${esc(s.at)} → ${esc(s.selector)}</code>`).join(", "));
  }
  parts.push('<section><div class="caveat">');
  parts.push(`<h2>${esc(c.title || "이 페이지가 말해 주지 못하는 것")}</h2>`);
  if (c.intro) parts.push(`<p>${c.intro}</p>`);
  parts.push("<ul>" + items.map((i) => `<li>${i}</li>`).join("") + "</ul>");
  parts.push("</div></section>");
}

parts.push("</div>");

fs.writeFileSync(outPath, parts.join("\n"));
console.log(`${outPath}: ${panels.length} panel(s) ` +
  `[${panels.map((p) => `${p.tag}@${p.ref}`).join(", ")}], ` +
  `${lifted.length} rule(s) lifted from ${path.basename(CSS)}`);

/* Shared fixture for the css-lift helpers — s172's JS and s169's Python must
   agree on every case here. Each case is a bug one of us actually shipped or
   nearly shipped, not a hypothetical.

   prefixes under test: [".zz-chip", ".zz-glyph"]
   body font under test: the `body` rule's font-family
*/

/* 1. plain, top level — lifted */
.zz-chip { color: #aaa; padding: 2px 6px; }

/* 2. prefix NOT first in the selector — lifted.
      s172's first hand-copy missed this whole shape. */
.zz-row:hover .zz-glyph { opacity: 1; }

/* 3. compound state rule — lifted.
      state is the subject of s169's specimen, so losing these loses the point. */
.zz-chip.zz-paused { color: #d29922; }

/* 4. a rule that mentions the prefix only in a later selector of the list */
.something-else, .zz-glyph { font-weight: 600; }

/* 5. INSIDE an at-rule — NOT lifted, and counted.
      s169 shipped this flat and it hid the specimen entirely:
      an unconditional `display: none`. */
@media (max-width: 820px) {
  .zz-chip { display: none; }
  .zz-glyph { font-size: 9px; }
}

/* 6. nested at-rules — still not lifted, counted once each */
@supports (display: grid) {
  @media (min-width: 1200px) {
    .zz-chip { letter-spacing: .02em; }
  }
}

/* 7. no prefix anywhere — not lifted, not counted */
.unrelated { color: red; }
#term-header { display: flex; }

/* 8. the inherited rule that reaches the specimen without naming it.
      s172's bug: SVG text has no font of its own and inherits from body, so
      lifting only prefixed rules typeset the specimen in the browser default.
      Must come back through the SEPARATE body-font path, not the prefix path. */
body {
  font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
  background: #14161a;
}

/* Runs the css-lift helpers out of render_diff.js against the shared fixture
   and compares to csslift_expected.json. The point of a SHARED fixture is
   that s169's Python must produce the same rows — a pin that only one
   implementation runs pins nothing about the pair. */
const fs = require("fs");
const src = fs.readFileSync("render_diff.js", "utf8");

/* Sliced by SPAN, not by function name. Brace-matched name-slicing (what
   render_diff's own `cutFn` and the repo's rolepanel_check do) cuts at the
   first `}` it sees and does not know it is inside a regex literal — these
   three helpers all contain one, so name-slicing produces a syntax error.
   That limitation is worth knowing about generally, not just here. */
const from = src.indexOf("function liftStyles(");
const to = src.indexOf("/* ---- rendering each panel");
const ctx = {};
new Function("exports",
  src.slice(from, to) + "Object.assign(exports,{liftStyles,liftBodyFont});")(ctx);

const css = fs.readFileSync("csslift_fixture.css", "utf8");
const want = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync("csslift_expected.json", "utf8"));

let bad = 0;
const eq = (what, got, exp) => {
  const a = JSON.stringify(got), b = JSON.stringify(exp);
  if (a === b) { console.log(`  ok   ${what}`); return; }
  bad++; console.log(`  FAIL ${what}\n       got ${a}\n       want ${b}`);
};

const { kept, skipped } = ctx.liftStyles(css, want.prefixes, false);
eq("lifted selectors", kept.map((r) => r.slice(0, r.indexOf("{")).trim()), want.lifted);
